    "minimal_shell_count": 4096,
    "minimal_shell_proof": "The unshifted raw construction has covolume 2^37: 4*Z_+^24 has covolume 2^49 and the 12-dimensional code reduces it by 2^12. Adding the shifted coset halves this to 2^36, and division by sqrt(8) in rank 24 gives covolume one. Every catalogue basis row belongs to the construction and its Gram determinant is one, so equal covolumes prove that the basis and two-coset models coincide. In the shifted coset every raw coordinate is odd, hence raw square at least 24 and lattice norm at least 3. Equality forces every coordinate to be +/-1, and the mod-4 residues give exactly one sign vector for each of the 4096 Golay codewords. In the unshifted coset, a nonzero codeword has weight at least 8; for codeword zero, the even-sum condition forces z^2 at least 2. Both cases have norm at least 4.",
